# Opinion

Meeting: 0002-bootstrap-rps-arena-platform
Agent: ArchitectB
Task: bootstrap RPS Arena platform
Context:
- Bootstrapping RPS Arena as a new project (separate from CalendarApp) with Node backend, MongoDB target, and stylized HTML5 front end.
- Modes: classic/extreme; variants: ranked/casual; features: matchmaking, ELO leaderboard/highscores, unlockables, Azure deployment.

Position:
- Bias toward home-grown orchestration (custom router, matchmaking queue, validation) to keep latency predictable and avoid framework overhead.
- Use repository abstraction to allow Mongo persistence while letting fast in-memory data power local dev and tests.

Recommendations:
- Keep a single domain model (users, matches, unlockables) flowing through services to avoid tight coupling between HTTP layer and storage.
- Treat unlockables/achievements as first-class artifacts stored with users so content expansion is easy without schema churn.
- Use GitHub Actions to enforce coverage and exercise the JS stack; future work can add health checks and Mongo migrations for Azure bootstraps.
